{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // The dead-export gate `npm run lint` enforces.
  //
  // `includeEntryExports` is kept, and it is NOT doing what this comment used to claim. Measured
  // against knip 6.32.2 on 2026-09-03 by appending a plainly dead `export const X = 1` to one file
  // at a time and re-running:
  //
  //   packages/tui/src/theme.ts            not an entry   -> REPORTED
  //   packages/agent/src/config/config.ts  not an entry   -> REPORTED
  //   packages/agent/src/index.ts          not an entry   -> REPORTED
  //   packages/tui/src/main.tsx            entry          -> not reported
  //   packages/cli/src/main.ts             entry          -> not reported
  //   packages/agent/src/chat-acp.ts       entry          -> not reported
  //   packages/tui/tools/render-banner.tsx entry          -> not reported
  //
  // The paths above are the ones that existed ON 2026-09-03 and are left as written. `theme.ts`
  // moved to `packages/tui/src/theme/theme.ts` on 2026-09-10, in the clipboard/theme fold.
  // Re-anchoring them would falsify the observation — rules/testing.md § 5: a live pointer is
  // re-anchored, a quotation of a measurement stays. Re-verified after the move by the same
  // method, and the answer is unchanged: a dead export in the new location is still REPORTED.
  //
  // Four for four: an export declared in an entry file is exempt anyway. Setting it here, setting it
  // inside a workspace block, and passing `--include-entry-exports` on the command line all produce
  // the same result. So the gate covers non-entry files — which is most of the tree, and includes
  // every barrel — and does not cover the four entry files.
  //
  // WHY, narrowed 2026-09-04 and filed as webpro-nl/knip#2011. It is not a knip 6.x regression and not
  // auto-discovery: `includeEntryExports` reports a dead entry export in a single package, with an
  // auto-discovered entry, and in a workspace — all three verified on 6.32.2. The trigger is a ROOT
  // `package.json` script naming a file inside a workspace. Two arms differing by one line:
  //
  //   "scripts": { "dev": "node packages/app/src/main.ts" }   present -> dead export NOT reported
  //                                                            absent -> dead export reported
  //
  // Which is exactly this tree: `"dev": "tsx packages/tui/src/main.tsx"`, `"exec": "tsx
  // packages/cli/src/main.ts"`, and `tools/build-cli.mjs`'s `entryPoints`. The workspace blocks below
  // declare `entry` as the TEST globs, so nothing else makes those files entries. knip also emits
  // `Remove redundant entry pattern` for the declaration that would have covered them, which is how
  // this stays invisible.
  //
  // WHAT HAPPENS WHEN THE FIX LANDS. webpro-nl/knip#2012 makes an EXPLICIT workspace `entry` win over
  // the script-derived exemption. Measured against that branch on this tree: the run goes from clean
  // to one finding —
  //
  //   packages/agent/src/hooks/fail-safe-defaults.test.ts:43  omittingAGateMustNotCompile
  //
  // — because the test globs below ARE declared entries, so their exports become checked. It is a true
  // positive and a deliberate survivor: a compile-time assertion helper, exported only because eslint
  // flags an unused local function, whose own docblock already says the scan would list it. The remedy
  // is local and verified on that branch: `"tags": ["-knipignore"]` here plus `/** @knipignore */` on
  // the symbol, which keeps the reason beside the code instead of in this file.
  //
  // The four `main`/entry FILES stay exempt even with that PR, because none of them is declared in any
  // `entry` below — only the root scripts make them entries. Adding them here would cover them once
  // the PR ships; it is deliberately NOT done yet, because the PR is unmerged and a config written for
  // an unreleased behaviour is a gate nobody can verify today.
  //
  // The claim this replaces was wrong twice over, and the second half is why it went unnoticed: it
  // said "every `index.ts` here is an entry", and no `index.ts` is in any entry list. The barrels are
  // covered precisely BECAUSE they are not entries. The "1 issue vs 28" measurement it cited was real
  // when written; what changed is knip, not this tree. The setting stays because it costs nothing and
  // becomes correct again the day the interaction is fixed upstream.
  //
  // Every package here is `private: true` and never published, so an export nobody imports has no
  // downstream consumer to protect: it is dead surface, not API. If a survivor must be kept, add it
  // to the workspace's `ignore` or `ignoreDependencies` WITH a comment saying why. An unexplained
  // exemption is how the previous cleanup (B-049) ended with 120 survivors and not one recorded
  // reason, which is what let the surface regrow unnoticed.
  //
  // WHAT THIS GATE CANNOT SEE — do not read a green run as more than it is. A dependency loaded
  // through a runtime-computed specifier is invisible to every static tool: `@theokit/tui` loads its
  // optional peers exactly that way (`const spec = "figlet"; await import(spec)`), and `lowlight`
  // is reached through `AgentTimeline` -> `ChatMessage` -> `MarkdownText` -> `CodeBlock`. Before
  // deleting any dependency, read the framework's own loaders and grep the shipped bundle by hand.

  "includeEntryExports": true,

  "workspaces": {
    // Only the test globs are listed. The other ten patterns this block used to carry were reported
    // by knip itself as `Remove redundant entry pattern` — it already reaches each of them without
    // being told: the four `tools/*.mjs` scripts and `.dependency-cruiser.cjs` through the
    // `package.json` scripts that run them, `vitest.config.ts` and `eslint.config.mjs` as tool
    // configs, and `src/main.ts` / `src/main.tsx` / `src/chat-acp.ts` through its default entry
    // patterns and the `build:acp` script. Verified by deleting them and re-running: still 0 issues,
    // and the same four files still resolve as entries.
    ".": {
      "entry": ["tools/**/*.test.mjs"],
      "project": ["tools/**/*.mjs", "*.ts", "*.mjs"],
      // B-136 — `@theokit/sdk` IS used, by `tools/build-cli.mjs`, and knip cannot see it: the
      // reference is `createRequire(import.meta.url).resolve('@theokit/sdk/package.json')`, which is
      // the runtime-computed specifier the note at the top of this file warns about. The build copies
      // `provider-catalog.json` out of that package, and without the copy auto-compaction is silently
      // disabled in every model mode.
      //
      // It is declared at the root because the root is what uses it. Nothing in `packages/*/src`
      // imports the SDK — it arrives under `@theokit/agents` as the pinned override — and the build
      // tool relying on that hoisting is what left `npm run build` unable to resolve it at all.
      // Recorded here rather than left as a standing warning, because a gate that always prints
      // something is a gate people stop reading.
      "ignoreDependencies": ["@theokit/sdk"],
    },
    "packages/agent": {
      "entry": ["tests/**/*.test.ts"],
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts", "tests/**/*.ts"],
    },
    "packages/cli": {
      "entry": ["tests/**/*.test.ts"],
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts", "tests/**/*.ts"],
    },
    "packages/tui": {
      "entry": ["tests/**/*.test.ts", "tests/**/*.test.tsx"],
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx", "tests/**/*.ts", "tests/**/*.tsx"],
    },
    "packages/shared": {
      "entry": ["tests/**/*.test.ts"],
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts", "tests/**/*.ts"],
    },
  },
}
